{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790361400,"nonce":"ROesbVUEmZIIY2JDQc59SwOdYL4=","title":"wasm: algebraic effects and fibers do not run","message":"The wasm entry points in crates/zyntax_wasm/src/lib.rs run the async and resumable-effect lowerings and execute the result in the bytecode interpreter. On that path nothing registers the `__zyntax_effect_*` symbols (`register_effect_runtime_symbols` and `register_fiber_runtime_symbols` in crates/zyntax_embed/src/effect_runtime.rs are `native`-only); the interpreter refuses `PerformEffect` and every raw fiber op (`hir_interp::instruction_name`) with no JIT tier to fall back to; the wasm backend has no arm for either; and `apply_krio_fiber_lowering` is never called. The async-handler driver (`__zyntax_effect_launch_handler`, `__zyntax_effect_finish_op`) and the timer drive inside `__zyntax_effect_resume` are compiled out on wasm32. Async functions do run: the JS event loop resolves host-bridge futures through `_zyntax_resolve_future` and `WASM_POLL_DISPATCH`.\n\nDone: the wasm runtime registers the effect runtime symbols and runs `PerformEffect` (static plus `lookup_op` dispatch) in the interpreter; fibers run behind `FiberCfg` through wasm stack switching or a stackless fallback, with `apply_krio_fiber_lowering` in the wasm pipeline; async handler operations launch through the wasm poll dispatcher.","files":null}]}